From a1e36334f096ce5268a7df2b750f1a4a09b83c52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:37:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 60/60] MAS local: type with the host input method in the
 emulator window

While the guest input method reports an editable text field, the window
is in text mode: the container, which has the keyboard focus, gets
WA_InputMethodEnabled, so the host's own input method works there, and
its composition reaches the guest as composing and committed text. Key
presses with printable text (AltGr included) are committed as text;
editing keys and Ctrl(+Shift)+letter go as Android key presses. Other
keys take the usual path. Leaving text mode resets an unfinished
composition, when it is ours. Windows only: elsewhere keycode forwarding
would still send typed keys to the guest as well.

Each key keeps the path its press took for its auto-repeats and its
release. Which presses are new comes from the WM_KEYDOWNs (lParam bit
30), which the native event filter queues for the key events: Qt calls
a held key's press new again after a modifier changes, and a new press
an auto-repeat after it missed a release (numpad keys with NumLock on,
whose key up the filter does not rename). Keys held down the usual way
are released when text mode starts, since the input method may take
their releases, and go the usual way again from their next auto-repeat
after it ends. A release the input method takes in text mode
(VK_PROCESSKEY, which Qt drops) is passed on from the native event
filter. With keycode forwarding on, the filter leaves the keys that text
mode may take to the key event, which forwards the others as the filter
would have.

In text mode the shortcut table no longer takes Ctrl(+Shift)+letter,
and Ctrl alone does not open the multi-touch overlay. Shortcuts on
editing keys (Ctrl+Backspace, Ctrl+arrows) still work. The input method
gets password and number hints from the inputType, and the guest's
cursor rectangle mapped back the way mouse events are mapped in.

Outside text mode keys, mouse and shortcuts behave as before.

Test: a fake guest input method reporting a focused field puts the
      window in text mode ('ime status' textmode=1) and closing it
      takes it out. Typing in the window was not tested here.
